    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0505" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2133<hi rendition="#superscript"
                    >10/18</hi></note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Statement Handed by the Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nomura</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State on May 23, 1941</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1941-05-23">May 23, 1941</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Errata for the Confidential
                        Memorandum</hi> [<hi rendition="#small-caps">of May</hi> 12, 1941]</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Read “amicable understanding” for “<hi rendition="#italic">entente
                            cordiale</hi>” in the 3rd paragraph of page 1.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Read the 2nd paragraph of page 4 as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“The Government of Japan maintains that the purpose of the Tripartite
                                Pact was, and is, defensive and designed to prevent the
                                participation of nations in the European War not at present involved
                                in it.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                    <pb facs="0506" n="440" xml:id="pg440"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Add to the last paragraph of Item IV (Page 6) as follows: <quote
                            rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“If a new commercial treaty is desired by both Governments, it would
                                be elaborated as soon as possible and concluded in accordance with
                                usual procedure.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
